---
import { canonicalUrl } from '../../../lib/site-origin.mjs';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8"/>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/>
<meta name="robots" content="index, follow"/><link rel="canonical" href={canonicalUrl('/tools/backup-restore-drill/')} />
<meta name="description" content="Private, vendor-neutral RTO and RPO backup restore drill planning tool."/>
<title>Backup restore drill planner | StackPilot AI</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/executive-theme.css" />
</head>
<body>
<a href="#main" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>
<header><nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
<a href="/">← StackPilot AI</a>
<a href="/guides/hosting-migration-checklist/">Hosting migration checklist</a>
<a href="/tools/hosting-cutover-gates/">Hosting cutover gates</a>
<a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>
</nav></header>
<main id="main">
<p>Private browser-only recovery planning</p>
<h1>Backup restore drill planner</h1>
<p>Compare the objectives you set with measurements you recorded from an authorized restore rehearsal. The numbers are <strong>user-entered, not independently verified</strong>. This is not a live backup, restore operation, recovery audit, uptime guarantee or approval for any production change.</p>
<p><strong>RTO</strong> is your maximum acceptable service restoration time. <strong>RPO</strong> is your maximum acceptable recovery-point age (the period of changes that might be lost). A backup timestamp and one restoration duration do not measure full application outage or actual data lost. Unknown measurements must stay blank, not zero.</p>
<form id="drill-form" novalidate>
<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="drill-title">
<h2 id="drill-title">Enter goals and rehearsal observations (minutes)</h2>
<div class="fields">
<label for="drill-targetRtoMinutes">RTO target — allowed restoration time in minutes
<input id="drill-targetRtoMinutes" name="targetRtoMinutes" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" value="120" required/></label>
<label for="drill-observedRestoreMinutes">Observed restore duration in minutes (leave blank if unknown)
<input id="drill-observedRestoreMinutes" name="observedRestoreMinutes" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" value="" /></label>
<label for="drill-targetRpoMinutes">RPO target — allowed recovery-point age in minutes
<input id="drill-targetRpoMinutes" name="targetRpoMinutes" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" value="60" required/></label>
<label for="drill-observedRecoveryPointAgeMinutes">Observed age of recovered point in minutes (leave blank if unknown)
<input id="drill-observedRecoveryPointAgeMinutes" name="observedRecoveryPointAgeMinutes" type="text" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" value="" /></label>
</div>
</section>
<fieldset class="panel">
<legend>Self-attested rehearsal checks</legend>
<label class="check" for="drill-restoreTested"><input id="drill-restoreTested" name="restoreTested" type="checkbox"/><span>I ran an authorized restore rehearsal and observed the result</span></label>
<label class="check" for="drill-dataIntegrityChecked"><input id="drill-dataIntegrityChecked" name="dataIntegrityChecked" type="checkbox"/><span>I checked recovered data integrity against an authorized reference</span></label>
<p>These checks record your own assertions only. An unchecked or unknown step blocks readiness. No backup, data or proof is uploaded.</p>
</fieldset>
<div class="actions"><button type="submit">Evaluate my drill observations</button><button type="reset" class="secondary">Clear worksheet</button></div>
</form>
<p id="drill-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="drill-report-title">
<h2 id="drill-report-title">Private, unverified recovery planning report</h2>
<label for="drill-report">Review before copying or saving</label>
<textarea id="drill-report" readonly placeholder="Run a planning evaluation to create a local-only report."></textarea>
<div class="actions"><button id="drill-copy" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Copy report</button><button id="drill-download" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Download offline CSV</button></div>
<p>Every number in the export is user-entered. A result of READY_FOR_HUMAN_REVIEW never overrides your real operations, security, legal or change-management signoffs.</p>
</section>
<section class="panel">
<h2>Before considering a real cutover</h2>
<ul>
<li>Rehearse restoration in an authorized isolated environment; confirm backup completeness, relevant dependencies, permissions and encryption-key access.</li>
<li>Measure end-to-end application availability separately from component restore time; confirm the recovery-point timestamp reflects the required datasets.</li>
<li>Keep real evidence, credentials and customer data inside your own authorized organization systems, not in this worksheet.</li>
</ul>
</section>
<p><strong>Privacy:</strong> This worksheet calculates inputs in your browser; they are not submitted to StackPilot. Netlify Web Analytics is documented as enabled at the hosting layer and may record page visits; it does not receive the form measurements. See <a href="/privacy/">privacy notes</a>.</p>
</main>
<footer><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> · <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure</a> · StackPilot AI private preview</footer>
<script>
import {assessBackupRestoreDrill,formatBackupRestoreDrillReport,formatBackupRestoreDrillCsv} from '../../../lib/backup-restore-drill.mjs';
const form=document.querySelector('#drill-form');
const status=document.querySelector('#drill-status');
const report=document.querySelector('#drill-report');
const copy=document.querySelector('#drill-copy');
const download=document.querySelector('#drill-download');
const numbers=['targetRtoMinutes','observedRestoreMinutes','targetRpoMinutes','observedRecoveryPointAgeMinutes'];
const flags=['restoreTested','dataIntegrityChecked'];
let last=null;
function invalidate(){last=null;report.value='';copy.disabled=true;download.disabled=true;}
form.addEventListener('input',()=>{invalidate();status.textContent='Measurements changed. Reevaluate before copying or saving.';});
form.addEventListener('change',()=>{invalidate();status.textContent='Rehearsal checks changed. Reevaluate before copying or saving.';});
form.addEventListener('reset',()=>{invalidate();status.textContent='Worksheet cleared.';});
form.addEventListener('submit',event=>{
 event.preventDefault();
 try{
  const input=Object.fromEntries([
   ...numbers.map(key=>[key,form.elements.namedItem(key).value]),
   ...flags.map(key=>[key,form.elements.namedItem(key).checked])
  ]);
  const current=assessBackupRestoreDrill(input);
  report.value=formatBackupRestoreDrillReport(current);
  last=current;copy.disabled=false;download.disabled=false;
  status.textContent=current.readiness==='NO_GO'
   ?'NO_GO — missing or out-of-target recovery evidence needs human review.'
   :'READY_FOR_HUMAN_REVIEW — this does not authorize a live cutover.';
 }catch(error){
  invalidate();status.textContent=error instanceof Error?error.message:'Check the inputs.';
 }
});
copy.addEventListener('click',async()=>{
 if(!last||!report.value)return;
 try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(report.value);status.textContent='Report copied.';}
 catch{report.focus();report.select();status.textContent='Clipboard unavailable. Select and copy manually.';}
});
download.addEventListener('click',()=>{
 if(!last||!report.value||download.disabled)return;
 try{
  const csv=formatBackupRestoreDrillCsv(last);
  const file=new Blob([csv],{type:'text/csv;charset=utf-8'});
  const url=URL.createObjectURL(file);
  const anchor=document.createElement('a');
  anchor.href=url;anchor.download='stackpilot-backup-restore-drill.csv';
  document.body.append(anchor);anchor.click();anchor.remove();
  setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),1000);
  status.textContent='Offline CSV saved to your device. No measurements were submitted.';
 }catch{
  invalidate();status.textContent='CSV export failed. Recheck inputs and regenerate.';
 }
});
</script>
</body></html>
